        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Dashboard: control hub — per-agent nesting, shared/private tabs, presence",
        "body": "# Dashboard: control hub — per-agent nesting, shared/private tabs, presence\n\n> The multi-agent, multi-operator half of the vision: organize the dashboard by which agent built what, keep some tabs private, and see who else is in the workspace live.\n\nCloses #101151, #101152, #101153. **Stacked on #101098** — targets `main` with a cumulative diff.\n\n## What's in this PR\n- **Per-agent nesting (#101151)** — group the tab strip by each tab's `createdBy` provenance, with a collapse/expand control to fold a whole agent's tabs away. Pure grouping over existing provenance.\n- **Shared/private tabs (#101152)** — a tab may be `private`, visible only to its owner (enforced server-side, below).\n- **Presence (#101153)** — a lightweight \"who's viewing this tab\" indicator over the existing broadcast path; the presence event carries `{ operator, tabSlug, at }` (id + tab only, never document state), ephemeral and never persisted.\n\n## Security (private tabs)\nVisibility is enforced **server-side**, not by hiding in the UI: every gateway response that serializes the workspace doc passes through `filterWorkspaceForOperator(doc, resolveOperatorIdentity(client))` (a `respondDoc` helper on `workspace.get`, every mutation response, `tab.create`, and `undo`), so a private tab the caller doesn't own is absent from the wire payload **and** the tab order. The store keeps the full doc; only the response is filtered. **Fail-closed:** an unidentified operator sees zero private tabs. (Operator identity is currently keyed on the paired **device id** — documented as the exact seam where a richer per-human identity threads in; a bootstrap-authed connection with no paired device can neither see nor own a private tab.)\n\n## Real behavior proof\n**Behavior or issue addressed:** With many agents and/or operators sharing one dashboard, there was no way to organize by agent, keep a tab private, or see concurrent activity. This adds per-agent grouping, server-enforced private tabs, and live presence.\n**Evidence:** `node scripts/test-projects.mjs extensions/dashboard` → 90 passed (visibility filter, fail-closed default, owner-only access, presence-payload shape — a private tab owned by A verified absent from B's serialized payload and tab order); `pnpm vitest run src/lib/dashboard src/pages/plugin` → 119 passed (actor grouping/fold, presence store TTL + self-exclusion, visibility round-trip); `ui:i18n:check`, `ui:build`, full type-aware oxlint clean.\n",
